    "statement": "For distinct product lifts and quotient lifts, the normalized coupling matrix satisfies exact product-direction and quotient-direction syzygies. After inverting two, the traditional joint ideal, one coupling row and column, and the full coupling rectangle are equal. Characteristic-zero zero entries form a partial matching, so at least mr-min(m,r) entries are nonzero, but the cross-generation equality proves they are not independent ideal generators.",
